t was ultimately deemed unsuitable. This indicates that while the transplantation was successfully carried out in 2003, it was not considered an appropriate option for the specific condition of MNGIE.", "MERCEDES VÁZQUEZ GUTIÉRREZ:Dra. Mercedes Vázquez Gutiérrez is a specialist in Endocrinology and Nutrition at the Hospital Universitario de Torrecárdenas in Almería.", "HOSPITAL UNIVERSITARIO DE TORRECÁRDENAS:Hospital Universitario de Torrecárdenas is a clinical unit specializing in Endocrinology and Nutrition located in Almería.", "PANCREATITIS AGUDA:Acute pancreatitis is a medical condition characterized by inflammation of the pancreas, which can lead to tissue damage and affect other organs. This condition often manifests with symptoms that arise between 24 and 36 hours following the peak production of cytokines. In the case of the patient, acute pancreatitis was experienced prior to the diagnosis of a tumor, necessitating intensive treatment and monitoring. Additionally, careful nutritional management is crucial for patients with acute pancreatitis, particularly for those who are diabetic.", "UCI:The Unidad de Cuidados Intensivos (UCI), also known as the Intensive Care Unit, is a specialized area within a hospital dedicated to providing critical care to patients facing severe health challenges. This unit is particularly equipped to manage patients with serious conditions, such as severe pancreatitis, and is designed to handle complications that may arise during treatment. Patients requiring intensive monitoring and advanced medical interventions are transferred to the UCI to ensure they receive the highest level of care during critical situations.", "DUODENOPANCREATECTOMÍA SUBTOTAL:Subtotal duodenopancreatectomy is the surgical procedure performed on the patient to address the pancreatic tumor.", "TAC:TAC, or Tomografía Axial Computarizada, is a medical imaging technique utilized to monitor a patient's condition over time, particularly for the detection of lesions. In this case, a CT scan was performed, revealing irregularities in the pancreatic process along with other findings. The procedure specifically aimed to confirm the dilation of the Wirsung duct in the patient, highlighting its importance in diagnosing and assessing pancreatic conditions.", "RMN:Magnetic Resonance Imaging (RMN) was conducted to suggest the presence of a mucinous tumor in the patient.", "BIOPSIA:A biopsy was performed via endoscopic ultrasound to confirm the diagnosis of the pancreatic mucinous tumor.", "HEMODIÁLISIS:Hemodialysis was required by the patient due to renal failure during their stay in the UCI.", "SANGRADO MASIVO:Massive bleeding occurred post-surgery, necessitating urgent intervention for the patient.", "DEHISCENCIA DE LA ANASTOMOSIS PANCREATOYEYUNAL:Dehiscence of the pancreatojejunostomy occurred, leading to further complications for the patient."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}